faqs:
  - question: Is rheumatoid arthritis the same as osteoarthritis?
    answer: >-
      No. Osteoarthritis is caused by wear and repair of the joints.
      Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune condition, where the immune system
      attacks the lining of the joints. It needs different treatment.
  - question: Can rheumatoid arthritis affect other parts of the body?
    answer: >-
      Yes. It can cause tiredness and affect the eyes, lungs, heart and blood
      vessels. It also raises the risk of heart disease, so looking after your
      heart matters.
